" change_id="Id3d8ef53b683fdd8f789246762c0d371ac53d438" commit="440b9a7ba1140adee696622440f328802500833b" commit_message="frecon: More style fixes  This fixes the pointer declarations to follow then chromium style.  BUG=none TEST=compiles  Change-Id: Id3d8ef53b683fdd8f789246762c0d371ac53d438 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/318311 Commit-Ready: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="318311" owner_email="marcheu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/frecon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/frecon" ref="refs/changes/11/318311/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie4b3b002c95b81f30c4c63799b77819651050757" commit="662a5038c438ccd23a5c7e72bd741b88cdeb9808" commit_message="gce_au_worker: Avoid using colon in file names  The `test_that` script uses colon as a seperator in autotest suite names, e.g., `test_that -b lakitu 1.1.1.1 suite:gce-smoke`. We used to use the full suite name as file name when saving test results, and it confused a piece of chromite code (chromite.commands.ListFailedTests, which uses a regular expression to match file names and colon is not deemed as a valid character) that parses test logs for failed tests.  A sample failure can be found here (notice the 'IndexError' at the bottom of the log): https://uberchromegw.corp.google.com/i/chromeos/builders/lakitu%20canary/builds/712/steps/GCETest%20%28attempt%202%29/logs/stdio  While we can change the chromite code to include colon, I think it's better to not use colon in file names at all, as it is commonly used as seperator in things like $PATH and URL.  This CL also tweaks VerifyImage to print out the summarized test report in case of a test failure, and includes some style smashes to better conform with the style guide.  BUG=b:25849966 TEST=Unit test. Also ran a trybot against lakitu-pre-cq, with an intentional     test failure and verified that failed test was correctly linked in the     buildbot log, and the 'IndexError' was gone.  Change-Id: Ie4b3b002c95b81f30c4c63799b77819651050757 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317781 Commit-Ready: Daniel Wang &lt;wonderfly@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Wang &lt;wonderfly@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Amey Deshpande &lt;ameyd@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317781" owner_email="wonderfly@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/crostestutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crostestutils" ref="refs/changes/81/317781/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I18e14b042c918080536bac44aef6c7856c82eeca" commit="28b2ae323d663c58ab4225811a7c39dd86a59996" commit_message="Marking 9999 ebuild for chromeos-base/chromeos-dbus-bindings as stable.  BUG=b:26092352 TEST=build packages  Change-Id: I18e14b042c918080536bac44aef6c7856c82eeca Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/318270 Commit-Ready: Daniel Colish &lt;colish@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Colish &lt;colish@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alex Vakulenko &lt;avakulenko@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="318270" owner_email="colish@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/70/318270/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7741.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>